To inject a custom correlation id in to the header before sending it upstream using the Kong API, you can use the "response" option in the "upstream" block of your configuration.

Here is an example of how you can use the "response" option to inject a custom correlation id in to the header:
```
upstream backend {
  server backend1.example.com;
  server backend2.example.com;
}

http {
  upstream_response_timeout 5m;

  # Inject custom correlation id in to the header
  map $http_response_header {
    "Correlation-Id" = "MyCustomCorrelationId";
  }

  # Set the upstream to your backend servers
  server {
    listen 80;
    server_name example.com;

    # Invoke the upstream
    invoke backend;
  }
}
```
In this example, the "map" directive is used to inject a custom correlation id in to the "Correlation-Id" header. The value of the custom correlation id is "MyCustomCorrelationId". This header will be sent upstream to your backend servers, allowing you to use it in your backend code.

