To make a picture rotate 360 degrees infinitely using CSS, you can use the `animation` property and the `rotate` function. Here is an example of the CSS code you can use:
```
@keyframes rotate {
 0% {
  transform: rotate(0deg);
 }
 100% {
  transform: rotate(360deg);
 }
}
```
To apply this animation to your picture, you would add a `class` or `id` to the `<img>` element and then use the `animation` property in your CSS to apply the `rotate` animation to that element. For example:
```
<img src="your-image.jpg" class="rotating-image">

.rotating-image {
  animation: rotate 10s infinite;
}
```
This would cause the image to rotate 360 degrees every 10 seconds, in an infinite loop. You can adjust the duration and timing function of the animation to suit your needs.
